            <ArticleTitle>Capsular 'pits' in the human lens.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The lens capsule is an atypical basement membrane surrounding the lens epithelial cells and lens fibres which make up the remainder of the human lens. A seemingly unreported morphological change visible in the lens capsule with the biomicroscope is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
